From f636b40e1d0ca0143daf2847e5452c3b39844329 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "kaijian.ding" <kaijian.ding@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 11:42:30 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 7/8] fix(google): keep thinking parts signed on the Claude
 wire
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two independent ways an unsigned thinking block reached Cloud Code, both of
which it rejects with "messages.N.content.N.thinking.signature: Field
required":

1. `reasoningPart()` returned the raw thought head verbatim whenever one
   existed, so the sidecar `googleThoughtSignature` never landed. Gemini
   streams thought text and its signature as separate parts (#3158), so a head
   captured before the signature arrived is unsigned even though the core holds
   it. The signature now falls back to the sidecar when the head has none.

2. A thought part that was never signed at all cannot be repaired here —
   `skip_thought_signature_validator` is not a signature on this wire (see
   ensureGoogleThoughtSignatures). For Claude the part is now dropped:
   thinking blocks are optional in history, so the turn stays legal.

`ensureGoogleClaudeWireOrder` becomes `ensureGoogleClaudeWireRules` since it
now owns both Claude wire invariants (tool_result pairing + thinking
signatures).

Live check against daily-cloudcode-pa.googleapis.com (claude-opus-5-5-low):
keeping the unsigned thought reproduces the reported 400 verbatim; dropping it
removes the thinking error and the turn proceeds.
